# Implementation Plan: Phase 8 - Outcome Dashboard Integration

## Goal
Connect the disparate "Clinical Components" in the Nucleus HUD to the real GentleQuest API.
Specifically, verify that [NucleusWellnessChart](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/tools/nucleus-hud/app/components/outcome/NucleusWellnessChart.tsx#14-94) renders real GAD-7/PHQ-9 data from the database.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> This integration requires the Nucleus HUD to have access to the GentleQuest API URL.
> Default is `http://localhost:5000` (Local) or Production URL.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Frontend Integration (`tools/nucleus-hud`)
- **Modify `NucleusWellnessChart.tsx`**:
    - Add `useEffect` to fetch data from `/api/assessment/history`.
    - Add `sessionId` input (or default to a known test session).
    - Transform API response (`[{type, score, timestamp}]`) to Chart Format (`[{name: "Date", score: 12}]`).
    - Support toggling between GAD-7 (Anxiety) and PHQ-9 (Depression).

### 2. Configuration
- Ensure `API_URL` environment variable is set correctly in HUD.

## Verification
- **Manual Test**:
    1. Submit a GAD-7 assessment via Postman/Curl (or the App).
    2. Open HUD `/clinical`.
    3. Verify the new point appears on the chart.
